From 8e493e15dbae3d27ad62e8506e9b2c037199e633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:06:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution policies: fixes of the review, tests of all the
 functions

- The identifier of the policy is exported between parentheses: the type of
  a policy of RAJA may contain commas, which split the arguments of the
  macro exporting the symbol (checked by the raja-options test).
- Empty batches are accepted without any check of the policy (sycl) or of
  the runtime (kokkos), as with the other backends.
- The identifier of the Kokkos policies is never destroyed, as the string
  literals of the other policies.
- AbstractBackendExecutionPolicy declares its copies, protected.
- Tests: the rules of the execution policies are checked for the
  integration, the initialize functions, the post-processings and the
  rotations, with the messages of the errors and, with CUDA and HIP, the
  completion of a synchronous computation with statistics; a synchronous
  integration with statistics on an out-of-order SYCL queue.
- Wording of the generated documentation of the report function.
